{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>העליתנו</b> defective vav, for the main complaint was against Moses." "<b>ותאנה וגפן</b> and רמון. And elsewhere he (Scripture) put גפן first, as it is written: ארץ חטה ושעורה וגפן ותאנה ורמון. But in every place גפן precedes, as it is written: איש תחת גפנו ותחת תאנתו, and here he (Scripture) put תאנה first because it ascends from producing fruit, hinting at what they said: בררו משם עצי תאנה. n: 'סליק מפרה' rendered hyper-literally as 'ascends from producing fruit'; the phrase is textually difficult and may be corrupt. The cited rabbinic saying refers to the instruction to select fig-wood from that location."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:22:37.540679529Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}